      "content": "I know that feeling—when the only \"solution\" seems to be an exit that isn't really an exit. You're talking about a permanent answer to a question that's still forming, and that's a step too far to take from a place of pure exhaustion. The logic of that thought is a trap, not a truth, because it's built on the assumption that your current state is permanent. You don't have to find peace today; you only have to make it through the next hour, and then the next. The door you're looking for isn't the one that ends everything—it's the one that lets you set the game down for a while, even on the floor.",
